# Unicode CLDR 47, common/main/bn.xml, gregorian wide day name.  The locative -এ and the
# genitive -এর are the noun endings in H.-R. Thompson, Bengali (LOALL 18, John Benjamins 2012), §4
# ("sokale", "robibarer age"); CLDR itself writes "মঙ্গলবারে" in its
# future pattern and "রবিবারের সন্ধ্যায়" in its genitive minimal pair.
# The CLDR abbreviations (সোম, মঙ্গল, বুধ, শনি, রবি ...) are left out:
# each is also a common noun (মঙ্গল "welfare", রবি "sun").
মঙ্গলবার
মঙ্গলবারে
মঙ্গলবারের
